SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Paraskevi\, Kato Chora
LOCATION:Kato Chora\, Serifos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Chora feast of high summer: vespers at Agia Paraskevi in Kato Chora on the evening of 25 July\, then food and wine from the ktitores and island dancing (syrto) in the lanes until late\, with liturgy next morning\; a second Agia Paraskevi feast is held at Galani the same night. Chora is car-free — park at the top by the windmills or below at Livadi and take the steps.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/serifos/#kato-chora-panigiri-of-agia-paraskevi-kato-chora
